#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""longhand-agent — the loop between today's note and the model.

    longhand-agent run --trigger <kind> [--hash <block>[,<block>…]] [--date YYYY.MM.DD]
    longhand-agent chat --hash <block> --message <text>         # dive in: continue that block's session
    longhand-agent ack --hash <block>                           # the student has seen the reply
    longhand-agent rate up|down|none --hash <block>             # the student's word on a reply (feedback.tsv)
    longhand-agent accept --hash <block> --index <n>            # run a proposal through the CLI
    longhand-agent tasks [--days 7]                             # open checkboxes across daily notes, JSON
    longhand-agent next [--days 7]                              # tasks (with their clock) + open suggestions/observations, JSON
    longhand-agent box keep|shelve --key <key>                  # a box kept on purpose, or not now (lifespan.py)
    longhand-agent plan [--force]                               # the planning job: do-dates and questions (plan.py)
    longhand-agent proposals                                    # what the agent proposes or asks, open, JSON
    longhand-agent proposal accept|decline|answer|applied|undo --id N [--answer TEXT]
    longhand-agent autonomy                                     # each kind of action: its level and its record, JSON
    longhand-agent dismiss --date D --kind suggestion|observation --index <n>
    longhand-agent curriculum                                   # convert PDFs in the curriculum folder to .md
    longhand-agent context --trigger <kind> [--hash <block>]   # payload only, no model
    longhand-agent state [--date YYYY.MM.DD]                    # today's state JSON
    longhand-agent stats [--days 14 | --since YYYY-MM-DD] [--json]   # how the tool is used
    longhand-agent projects                                     # the tags that exist, with their next session
    longhand-agent project --tag T [--name N]                   # make a project: its file in knowledge/projects/
    longhand-agent timetable [--fetch [--index n]]              # each calendar's state, for the Settings sheet, JSON
    longhand-agent eval add <payload> [--job margin|plan|day|talk]   # a real run made into an eval case (in the vault)
    longhand-agent eval run [--model M] [--case ID]             # the cases against the repo's prompts; kept as history
    longhand-agent eval status                                  # which prompt and model have passed
    longhand-agent review [--write | --if-due]                  # the week of the agent, for the student to read
    longhand-agent documents [--tag T]                          # filed course documents (projects/<tag>/docs/), JSON
    longhand-agent notebook [forget|correct|take-back] [--file F --text T [--to N] | --n K]
                                                                # what the agent knows, and the student's corrections
    longhand-agent search [--folders | --words W [--folder F] | --file F]   # what the day's agent may search, JSON
    longhand-agent day --message M [--block HASH]               # the day's conversation: talk to the day, not a line
    longhand-agent install [--force]                            # opencode agent defs (checked by their evals) + dirs

One pass, then exit. Nothing is resident. The model gets no tools: everything
it may see is assembled here from an allowlist (today's note minus private
blocks, the agent's own knowledge files, the curriculum folder, the timer and
deadline report, the next two weeks of the timetable), logged verbatim to the payload log before inference, and
everything it says back is applied here — transcript, state file, knowledge
files, cost ledger. No code path in this file opens anything under the daily
notes folder for writing, nor anything under the notes root (`human/` here,
docs/files.md); `guard_write` enforces that.

Config: ~/.config/longhand/config.json (see config.example.json).
"""
